2c. 1991 fake zeros: all sources zero yet drnk_wat_f == 1
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   src_allzero91 drnk_wat_f      N
          <lgcl>      <num>  <int>
1:         FALSE         NA      4
2:         FALSE          0     40
3:         FALSE          1 555745
4:          TRUE         NA    434
5:          TRUE          0   1219
6:          TRUE          1   7413

src_allzero_wat91 == TRUE for 7,413 shrids.

WHY THIS MATTERS. PHASE0_SPEC.md 3.3's missingness rule only covers rows
where pc91_vd_drnk_wat_f is MISSING. These rows are not missing: the flag
says 1 (drinking water IS available) while all nine source variables are
coded 0. The spec's rule does NOT protect them. Under the missing=0
version they receive tap = 0 and private_gw = 0, but they are likely FAKE
ZEROS -- water present, source not recorded.

HANDLING: the flag src_allzero_wat91 is carried into the output. These
rows are NOT dropped by default. Section 2e reports how every 1991
outcome changes when they are excluded, so the sensitivity is visible
without baking a choice into the data.

NOTE: the analogous flag is degenerate for 2001/2011, where the anchor is
CONSTRUCTED from the sources -- an all-zero row there has drnk_wat_f == 0
by construction, so 'all zero yet flag == 1' cannot occur. Not built.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2d. Outcome construction
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Shares: tap91_share and tap01_share are built from village COUNTS.
tap11_share is NA by construction -- the 2011 source variable is binary
(max rule), so the intensive margin does not exist in the data.
private_gw *_share is not built in any year: it is an OR of two counts,
and the union of the two village sets is not recoverable from the counts.

